# Publisher -- excluded from every Docker build context (Dockerfile.api,
# Dockerfile.worker). Both Dockerfiles COPY entire directory trees
# (`COPY services/ services/`, etc.) rather than cherry-picking files, so
# this is what keeps test-only code out of the shipped images.
#
# E6.1 (docs/ARCHITECTURE_SCORE_10_PLAN.md) -- this specifically closes a
# real gap, not a hygiene nicety: Dockerfile.worker's PYTHONPATH lists each
# service's ROOT (e.g. /app/services/structure), not something narrower like
# a site-packages directory. Python 3's implicit namespace packages (PEP
# 420, no __init__.py required) mean that without this file,
# `services/structure/tests/` would be importable inside the worker
# container as `import tests` purely because it sits next to
# `publisher_structure/` on a PYTHONPATH entry -- regardless of the fact
# that `tests/` is never `pip install`ed (see each service's own
# pyproject.toml, which only includes `publisher_*`). That would make
# services/structure/tests/fabricating_provider.py importable in production,
# defeating the entire point of moving it out of publisher_structure/.
**/tests/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
